  "notes": [
    "DEMO CATALOGUE — NOT OFFICIAL PRICING. Every amount below was read from the screenshots supplied with this internship project. None of it is authorised by Zoho or Site24x7 and none of it may be presented to a buyer as a binding price.",
    "The supplied sources disagree with each other. The Zoho Store comparison (pricingall.pdf) and the account-specific 'Personalized Plans' page (personalizedplans.jpeg) give different figures for the same plan names, and the generated quote (quote.png) shows a third set. Across every plan the quote figures are exactly 18/19 of the store list price (for example 9,720 / 10,260 and 44,910 / 47,405), which looks like a promotional or account-level discount. The discount is NOT implemented: this project does not invent discounts.",
    "Catalogue values use the Zoho Store comparison because it is the only source that gives plans, entitlements and add-on packs in one internally consistent capture.",
    "Add-on pack prices vary by plan tier in pricingall.pdf. This demo applies one observed pack-price set across all plans that allow add-ons. Plan-specific add-on pricing needs the authorised price book.",
    "Included RUM pageviews and AppLogs volume for the Enterprise plan were not visible in any supplied source. They are set to 0 so that demand is priced through add-on packs — the conservative assumption, because it can only overstate cost, never understate it."
  ],
